## Third-party components

| Component | License | How it is used |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) | MIT | vendored source, compiled into `liblocalmind.so` (clone it into `third_party/llama.cpp`) |
| [AirLLM](https://github.com/lyogavin/airllm) | Apache-2.0 | **idea only** — memory-budget planning and disk-streamed weight loading reimplemented natively for Android; see `docs/AIRLLM.md` and `third_party/airllm-reference/` |
| [liuran001/WeChat-LiquidGlass](https://github.com/liuran001/WeChat-LiquidGlass) | see upstream | **technique reference only** — the liquid-glass bottom bar in this app (floating pill, backdrop capture + stack blur, spring-driven indicator) is an independent Kotlin/Compose reimplementation inspired by its approach. No code copied. |
| [xiaojiaenen/liquid-glass](https://github.com/xiaojiaenen/liquid-glass) | see upstream | **design reference only** — Apple "Liquid Glass" parameters (tint layering, specular highlight). React/SVG source, not usable on Android. |
| AndroidX / Jetpack Compose | Apache-2.0 | UI |
| OkHttp | Apache-2.0 | model downloads |
| kotlinx.serialization / coroutines | Apache-2.0 | persistence / async |

Model weights are **not** distributed with this project. Every catalogue entry links to its
original repository and lists its license (Apache-2.0, Llama-3.2-Community, Gemma, MIT, …);
downloading a model means accepting that model's own license.
